@[Welcome to the SMGL @ENCHANT_ISO_VERSION@ install iso!]
This is the guided shell prompt enchantment (installer).

To see the list of all steps: @[list] (or @[steps]).
To see the list of all commands: @[help]. To show the current step's
instructions again: @[todo].
To see this message again: @[welcome].

To set a different keymap: @[keymap]
  (or @[539], which types the same on any keyboard layout).

On a laptop? @[acpi -b] shows the battery charge; keep an eye on it.

No network is needed to install. To get online anyway (@[ip link] lists the
network interfaces; replace wlan0 below with yours):
  wired:  @[dhcpcd]
  Wi-Fi:  @[wpa_passphrase 'NETWORK' 'PASSWORD' > /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf]
          @[wpa_supplicant -B -i wlan0 -c /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf]
          @[dhcpcd wlan0]
The installed system has the same tools (copy /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf over).
To install from another computer over SSH instead, run these three commands:
  @[passwd]                                  (set a root password)
  @[ssh-keygen -A]                           (create the host keys)
  @[/usr/sbin/sshd -o PermitRootLogin=yes]   (start the SSH server)
then on the other computer: @[ssh root@ADDRESS] (@[ip addr] shows this
machine's address). The host keys are new at every boot, so after a reboot
ssh warns "REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED"; that is expected here:
forget the old key there with @[ssh-keygen -R ADDRESS] and connect again.

If you have any feedback for us, please drop by #sourcemage-cauldron
